      en: "Kibbutz Lotan is a socialist community in southern Israel's Arava desert, founded in 1983. It is known for its commitment to ecological sustainability and permaculture. It runs a Center for Creative Ecology offering workshops on green building, solar energy, and organic farming. The community lives from agriculture, especially dates, and ecotourism. A birdwatching area attracts ornithologists. Lotan is a member of the Global Ecovillage Network and has about 150 members. Buildings are made from sustainable materials like mud and straw.",
